Dear Rue,

 Thank you for this! So, I did run a case with .01 (same configuration- 2 threads). It ran for 12 hours and then crashed with the same error (as before) after it finished calculating corrected std for hyper-parameters. I am attaching here the output file. I am running a case with more aggressive approximation of the Foot using .05 and using 'besag + iid: bym' model. Problem is aggressive approximation on Foot makes: Foot_approx * emission ~ observations_approx,  very different than the original one.

  I have some questions. I will really appreciate your kind help:

  1) Did the crash occur for same reason?
  2) Is there anything we could do (like changing to more informative priors or tolerance or something else) to make it run/converge faster as it is taking 15-20 hours. If yes, how can I do this?

Thanks,
Subhomoy

