On 22 Mar 2017, at 13:43, Paul Lantos <paul....@gmail.com> wrote:

> Also - just to clarify, in the prediction stack I'd add link=1 if I want predictions based on the fitted values in stack 1?

No quite. See below.

> So stack 1 has link=1, stack 2 has link=2,

Yes.

> and the prediction stack has link=1 ?

If your predictions relate to the first likelihood, then yes.
If they relate to likelihood 2, then use link=2. If some refer to 1 and some to 2, then supply a vector with 1s and 2s corresponding to each prediction.

Finn

