I'm travelling and adding this feature will have to wait a bit [there
are simply to many details in the general case]. If you need something
in a hurry, you can just use the Gaussian approximation, for which you
need the mean and covariance. and you can easily write your own version
returning also the logdens.
if you read the code in inla.hyperpar.sample, it should be clear. just
ignore the stdev.corr... stuff [set them to 1].

H

